{%- comment -%}
  Shared markup is prepended to every view layout before rendering, so the
  assigns below are in scope for all four layouts.

  Polled responses (see settings.yml polling_url):
    IDX_0 = /users/me
    IDX_1 = the open backlog the stats are computed from (window of 100)
    IDX_2 = closed-today count (only pagination.total_items is read)
    IDX_3 = today's activity across all visible workspaces

  Accuracy note: open_total, closed_today and activity_total come from
  pagination.total_items and are exact for any backlog size. due_today_count and
  overdue_count are counted from the 100-item window, so they are exact only
  while the scope query returns 100 items or fewer — which the default
  per-assignee query always will.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign me = IDX_0.data -%}
{%- assign open_items = IDX_1.data -%}
{%- assign open_total = IDX_1.pagination.total_items -%}
{%- assign closed_today = IDX_2.pagination.total_items -%}
{%- assign activity = IDX_3.data -%}
{%- assign activity_total = IDX_3.pagination.total_items -%}

{%- comment -%}
  A failed poll yields {} rather than an exception, so an unreachable server
  or a rejected query would otherwise render as a silently blank screen. The
  device has no logs to check, so name the fault on the screen itself.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign fault = '' -%}
{%- unless me.id -%}
  {%- assign fault = 'Cannot reach Windshift. Check the server URL and API token.' -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- if fault == '' -%}
  {%- unless IDX_1.pagination -%}
    {%- assign fault = 'Windshift rejected the scope query. Check the QL syntax.' -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Dates arrive as RFC 3339. Collapsing them to a YYYYMMDD integer makes the
  comparisons unambiguous, and a missing due date lands on 0 — which is never
  "overdue", because every real date compares greater.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign today_num = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 -%}

{%- comment -%}
  A single pass over the backlog produces every counter the layouts need.
  next_up is the soonest-due item that is not already overdue.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign overdue_count = 0 -%}
{%- assign due_today_count = 0 -%}
{%- assign next_up_num = 99999999 -%}
{%- assign next_up_found = false -%}
{%- for item in open_items -%}
  {%- assign due_num = item.due_date | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- if due_num > 0 -%}
    {%- if due_num < today_num -%}
      {%- assign overdue_count = overdue_count | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- if due_num == today_num -%}
        {%- assign due_today_count = due_today_count | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if due_num < next_up_num -%}
        {%- assign next_up_num = due_num -%}
        {%- assign next_up = item -%}
        {%- assign next_up_found = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%}
  With no due dates anywhere, fall back to the most recently touched item so
  the "Next up" slot still says something useful.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- unless next_up_found -%}{%- assign next_up = open_items | first -%}{%- endunless -%}

{%- assign owner_name = me.first_name -%}
{%- if owner_name == blank -%}{%- assign owner_name = me.full_name | split: ' ' | first -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if owner_name == blank -%}{%- assign owner_name = me.username -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} Centred message, used for the fault state. {%- endcomment -%}
{% template notice %}
  <div class="layout layout--col layout--center">
    <span class="value value--small">{{ headline }}</span>
    <span class="label">{{ detail }}</span>
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}

{%- comment -%} One stat tile. {% render %} is scope-isolated, so pass everything in. {%- endcomment -%}
{% template stat %}
  <div class="item">
    <div class="content">
      <span class="value value--{{ size | default: 'base' }} value--tnums">{{ number }}</span>
      <span class="label label--small">{{ caption }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}
